      "name": "FeCrAlTiSi multicomponent alloy",
      "material_category": "ferritic multicomponent alloy",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 1,
          "section": "Abstract",
          "quote": "We design and investigate a ferritic multicomponent alloy with high electrical resistivity, low temperature coefficient of resistivity (TCR) in a wide-temperature range, high strength, and moderate deformability",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "9044037e79625ee5:part:001"
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "section": "1. Introduction",
          "quote": "we then design a novel ferritic multicomponent alloy with enhanced resistivity and mechanical properties by integrating minor alloying elements (i.e., Ti and Si) into a ferritic matrix composed of multiple principal elements (i.e., Fe, Cr and Al).",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "9044037e79625ee5:part:001"
        }
      ]
    },
